      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define staffing, volunteer needs, and onboarding approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 58895,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, following our charter discussion, I've drafted the Staffing and Volunteer Recruitment Plan (A2) and an outline for the Volunteer Onboarding pack (A5). My initial thought for T2 is that we'll need 4-5 volunteers per event. Please review and share your feedback, especially on the training topics in A5.",
            "mentions": [
              76651,
              523420,
              41244
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A5",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 76651,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Thanks @58895, this is very helpful. For the first few events, I think 4 volunteers is a good minimum number: two for welcoming people and two to help run the actual activities. 5 would be ideal to have a floater.",
            "mentions": [
              58895
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 41244,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Can we manage with 3? We need to keep costs down, and volunteer management takes time.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 523420,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Three could be risky if someone calls in sick on the day. Having at least one backup seems wise.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 58895,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "I agree with both of you. @76651's point about the roles is spot on, and @523420 is right about contingency. How about this: we aim to recruit 5 volunteers per event, with the understanding that 4 is the minimum to proceed. This gives us a buffer. I've added this detail to A2.",
            "mentions": [
              76651,
              523420
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 41244,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Okay, that's a reasonable compromise. Let's agree on needing a minimum of 4 volunteers, aiming for 5, for the first three events.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 58895,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Perfect. Now, regarding the onboarding flow and training topics in A5 for T8. I've included safeguarding, data privacy, and our program's mission. What else is critical for them to know before day one?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 76651,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "We should definitely include a section on their specific roles during the event. A quick run-down of the schedule and who to contact if there's an issue.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 99312,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "A one-pager on key messages would be useful. Just a few bullet points on how to describe the program if people ask. It ensures we're all saying the same thing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 393987,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "Do they need to know about the data collection?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 58895,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Yes, absolutely. Great points everyone. I'll add three sections to the A5 training outline: 1. Event-specific roles & schedule, 2. Key communications messages, and 3. A simple guide on data collection ethics and methods. Thanks for the input.",
            "mentions": [
              76651,
              99312,
              393987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 41244,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "This sounds comprehensive. Let's approve this onboarding flow and the training topics.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
